.IX Title "Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger \- Consolidate index segments in the background.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 4
\&    my $bg_merger = Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger\->new(
\&        index  => \*(Aq/path/to/index\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&    $bg_merger\->commit;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Adding documents to an index is usually fast, but every once in a while the
index must be compacted and an update takes substantially longer to
complete.  See FastUpdates for how to use this class to control
worst-case index update performance.
.PP
As with Indexer, see FileLocking if your index is on a
shared volume.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 4
\&    my $bg_merger = Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger\->new(
\&        index   => \*(Aq/path/to/index\*(Aq,    # required
\&        manager => $manager             # default: created internally
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Open a new BackgroundMerger.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBindex\fR \- Either a string filepath or a Folder.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBmanager\fR \- An IndexManager.  If not supplied, an IndexManager with
a 10\-second write lock timeout will be created.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS optimize
.IX Subsection "optimize"
.Vb 1
\&    $background_merger\->optimize();
.Ve
.PP
Optimize the index for search-time performance.  This may take a
while, as it can involve rewriting large amounts of data.
.SS commit
.IX Subsection "commit"
.Vb 1
\&    $background_merger\->commit();
.Ve
.PP
Commit any changes made to the index.  Until this is called, none of
the changes made during an indexing session are permanent.
.PP
Calls \fBprepare_commit()\fR implicitly if it has not already been called.
.SS prepare_commit
.IX Subsection "prepare_commit"
.Vb 1
\&    $background_merger\->prepare_commit();
.Ve
.PP
Perform the expensive setup for \fBcommit()\fR in advance, so that \fBcommit()\fR
completes quickly.
.PP
Towards the end of \fBprepare_commit()\fR, the BackgroundMerger attempts to
re-acquire the write lock, which is then held until \fBcommit()\fR finishes
and releases it.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Index::BackgroundMerger isa Clownfish::Obj.
